   ],
   "tuning": [],
   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "them:minmax",
    "number": "Theorem 4",
    "quote": "For any $m\\le n$ and any $\\eps\\in(0,1)$, the error probability of SH for identifying an $(m,\\eps)$-good arm satisfies $\\pp{\\mu_{J_T}<\\mu_m-\\eps}\\le\\log_2n\\cd\\ep{-\\textup{const}\\cd m\\cd\\rbr{\\fr{\\eps^2T}{4n\\log_2^2(2m)\\log_2n}-\\ln(4e)}}$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Second part: for T >= c1 (ln(4e)+lnln n) n log2^2(2m) log2 n / eps^2, error <= exp(-Theta_tilde(m eps^2 T/n)). Theorem 8 restates this as a min over (m', eps')."
  },
